WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.210
- Hi, I'm Amy,

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:03.920
and this is a delicious
French pastry known

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.410
as a croquembouche.

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:07.900
As you can see, this is
one of the most beautiful

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.500
but technical and
labor-intensive desserts around.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.010
Today, I'm gonna attempt to make something

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.350
that has never been done before.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:18.190
I'm gonna attempt to make
a giant, doughy, cheesy,

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:21.040
rich, insane-looking croquembouche.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.570
Is it even possible to
turn this sweet delicacy

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:24.990
into a savory delight?

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:28.119
I have no idea, but I'm
willing to give it my all.

00:00:28.119 --> 00:00:30.702
(upbeat music)

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:44.820
So kicking things off,

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:46.820
I'm gonna start with
making my dough recipe.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:49.480
We've got our bread flour,
instant yeast, sugar,

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.280
just to get the yeast
going, and salt for taste.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.540
So I just mix that up until
it's nicely distributed.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:58.750
I'm gonna pop the oil in the
water, which is room temp.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.780
Stir that all together until
we have a nice shaggy dough.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.450
So I'm hoping to recreate a similar look

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:06.140
to a traditional croquembouche,

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.170
but this is gonna be made of bread dough.

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:10.090
Just love the smell of
yeast. Is that weird?

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.210
And now that's kind of come together,

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:12.560
I'll give it a whizz in the mixer.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:14.910
If you don't have a mixer,
that's absolutely fine.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.150
You can just do it by hand.

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:18.130
So I'm looking for the
dough to be nice and elastic

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:18.963
at this point.

00:01:18.963 --> 00:01:20.200
Warm.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.060
Lightly flour the surface,
just so it doesn't stick.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:25.140
But I don't wanna add too much flour

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.770
because it will change
the ratio of the dough.

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:32.220
I love kneading to get any tension out.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:36.310
You just give the dough a real good slap,

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:39.270
then you roll it forward, and
then pull it back over itself.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.640
So, you know your dough is
ready when you can roll it

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:44.490
into a ball, give it a bit of a knuckle,

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.570
and the dimple bounces back.

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:49.860
Yay! Put a little bit of
olive oil in this bowl.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.720
Pop this in here and give it a turn.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.540
Got your little baby dough ball.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:56.810
You have to nurture it,
massage it, love the dough.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:58.857
And cover this now. Just
prevents it from drying out.

00:01:58.857 --> 00:02:00.900
And we're gonna leave
that somewhere fairly warm

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.718
to double in size for about an hour.

00:02:02.718 --> 00:02:04.200
(relaxing music)

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.020
So now our baby is all grown up.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:08.530
It's time to stuff them with some cheese.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:10.520
Ooh! Look at that.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:13.590
Flour the surface a little,
and then pour her out.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:16.810
Just for ease, I'm gonna
cut this dough into four

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:18.880
and just work with one quarter at a time.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:20.320
Roll this into a sausage.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:23.550
Nice sausage. And then just
chop him into bite sized chunks.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:26.200
So I'm gonna take a
small chunk of cheddar.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.190
I'm using vegan cheddar,

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:29.570
but you can use any hard,
melting cheese that you like.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:30.540
Pop it in the middle.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:34.060
Pinch the edges to close it
like a little tiny envelope.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:35.550
And give it a roll.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:38.510
1 down, 149 to go.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:41.460
So this part of the recipe,
this is my bread and butter.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.190
I know how to make this.

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:46.810
But all the next steps, I
have never done that before.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:49.000
So this is the calm before the storm.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.980
Each of these are about the
size of a ping pong ball,

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.130
and I'm stuffing them with
about a teaspoon of cheese.

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:55.060
I'm leaving about an
inch between each ball

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:56.440
because they're gonna rise.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.910
Okay, this is taking a while,

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.350
but I do have some friends that can help.

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:02.320
Kelly and Mimo?

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.200
- You weigh, I'll stuff.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.340
- Okay. Wow. Look at you.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.040
Well done, guys. Super quick.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.240
Now it's time to glaze.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:10.870
Traditionally, egg wash is egg,

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.250
but I'm making a vegan version.

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:15.900
So I'm gonna mix almond milk
with a touch of maple syrup.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:19.870
Give that a whisk with
this teeny tiny whisk

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:21.320
and teeny tiny jug.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.650
I love painting, so I feel quite at home.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:24.900
So far so good.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.180
So now these are ready to bake.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.100
I'm gonna throw them in
the oven at full whack.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.110
475 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:31.690
These were in the oven
for about five minutes.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:34.400
They're nice and golden.
These look perfect.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.910
So now we're getting to the tricky part.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:37.070
A traditional croquembouche

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.060
has spun sugar all the way around.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.230
I'm doing a savory version,

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:43.900
so I'm gonna try and recreate
that same look with cheese.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.420
So to get started with this,
we're gonna do a little test.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.810
We have these various different cheeses.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:50.750
I don't know how they're gonna act.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.810
I'm just gonna test them and
see which is the most stringy.

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:57.280
So this is supposed to
be a parmesan. Parmesan.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.080
We're gonna go ahead and do
the same with mozzarella.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:01.260
The cheddar shreds, okay.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:04.310
I like how this is a
little rainbow of cheese.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.600
So I'm hoping that when these are melted,

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.910
I'll be able to pull them
into beautiful ribbons

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:10.270
and wrap them around the tower.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.780
Almost like wrapping lights
around a Christmas tree.

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:14.760
Okay, so now we've got all
the cheese on the baking tray.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.700
We're gonna melt it. Or try and melt it.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.576
We're gonna see what happens
when this goes in the oven.

00:04:18.576 --> 00:04:20.150
(upbeat drum music)

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:21.880
So now my cheese is melting.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:23.960
I'm gonna try and
construct a mini tower just

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:26.502
to see what I've got myself in for.

00:04:26.502 --> 00:04:29.502
(mischievous music)

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:34.410
I think this might be
harder than anticipated.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:37.540
I'm hoping that the cheese
will help to glue this together

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:40.700
because at the moment, it's
not a very stable structure.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:45.520
It works stacking a mini tower,
but I'm gonna try doing 150,

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:48.503
and I feel like gravity is
gonna conspire against me.

00:04:50.127 --> 00:04:53.187
(tense music)

00:04:53.187 --> 00:04:56.270
Hmm. Varying degrees of success here.

00:04:57.490 --> 00:04:59.800
This I can't even take off of the tray.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.020
This is just a gluey mess.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:03.810
This is bad. You cannot pick this up.

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:07.120
This one just barely even melted.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.560
It's retained all of its structure.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:13.130
The most promising is probably this one,

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:15.460
but it's the best of a bad bunch.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.020
No, this hasn't worked.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:19.290
This is just a big sticky, ugly mess.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:20.490
So this was a fail.

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:22.600
It's time to go back to the drawing board.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:23.433
Whilst I was happy

00:05:23.433 --> 00:05:25.350
with how the dough balls
resembled cream puffs

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:27.060
of a traditional croquembouche,

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:29.240
I was losing faith in my ability

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:31.110
to pull off the rest of the elements.

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:32.800
How are these gonna stack?

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:35.620
What can I add to make
this taste delicious?

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:38.400
Also, this needs to look amazing.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.330
I buckled down and did some research,

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:41.900
mocked up a few sketches,

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.320
scanned the Tasty kitchen, and
came up with some new ideas

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.520
with a new found sense of optimism.

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:48.630
So instead of melting it to make ribbons,

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:51.330
I'm thinking if I melt the cheese

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:52.870
and put it in a piping bag,

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:56.420
I'll be able to precisely pipe strands.

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:57.253
Let's try it.

00:05:57.253 --> 00:05:58.340
So I've got some cheddar here.

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:02.100
I'm gonna pop it in the pan
and melt it over a low heat.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:05.170
I'm hoping it'll turn into
like a cheese fondue situation.

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:06.730
It's melted well.

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:10.310
It's feeling kind of
gluey, but gluey is good.

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:11.880
So I'm gonna put this in the piping bag

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:13.880
and test it on a new mini tower.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:15.770
Normally I'm used to
doing this with icing,

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:17.870
but this is my first time piping cheese.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:19.850
Let's see if this cheese can
stick two balls together.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:23.660
Mm. Okay. Looking promising.

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:25.510
Okay, so two have worked.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:29.010
I'm feeling like I should
lay it like bricks,

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:30.510
sort of stagger them.

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:31.620
I'm not an engineer,

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.030
but I feel like doing it like this

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:35.960
will give it the most
structural integrity.

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:37.360
On a traditional croquembouche,

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:39.960
spun sugar, in addition
to being an adhesive,

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:42.428
adds a bit of pizazz, a
bit of je nais sais quois,

00:06:42.428 --> 00:06:43.955
a little bit of razzle dazzle.

00:06:43.955 --> 00:06:45.214
(record scratches)

00:06:45.214 --> 00:06:47.920
(groans) I'm sorry.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:50.800
This is like the ugliest
wedding cake I've ever seen.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:52.820
So this color is kind of cartoonish.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:55.160
This looks like a cheesy nightmare.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:57.550
This is not what we're going for.

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:02.550
This piping started promising
but ended in a disaster.

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:09.280
This is not the savory
croquembouche of my dreams.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.750
(upbeat medieval music)

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:14.580
Okay, so I have a new plan
and this time it's gonna work.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:18.010
This new plan will combine
style, substance, function.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:21.030
The new plan is parmesan crisps.

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:23.080
I feel like these are gonna
elevate the whole look

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:23.913
of the tower.

00:07:23.913 --> 00:07:28.080
Sprinkle a touch of parmesan
in these mini circles

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.420
to make these lacey crisps.

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:33.640
I'm just gonna bake these on
350 degrees Fahrenheit just

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:35.010
for a couple of minutes
until they're brown

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:36.700
around the edges.

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:38.290
Okay, so these look good.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:40.810
I'm just gonna jimmy this under this guy.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:43.750
And I feel like I should
be able to manipulate this

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:46.380
into a nice sort of flower shape.

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:49.320
Just gives it more texture. So cute.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:51.110
I'm just gonna keep placing these around,

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:52.694
fill in all the gaps.

00:07:52.694 --> 00:07:54.220
I'm liking the look of this.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:55.280
I'm happy with this.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.500
I feel like it's not all the way there,

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:00.810
but I think this will
work on a bigger scale,

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:02.440
especially as I'm gonna combine it

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:04.360
with two extra ideas that I have.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:06.540
So I'm gonna take all of these balls

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:10.740
and attempt to make my
giant cheesy croquembouche.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:12.370
(upbeat jazz music)

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:14.430
So I'm feeling good about
those parmesan crisps.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:17.890
But what is a dough ball
without garlic butter? Nothing.

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:20.250
So I'm gonna go ahead and
make the garlic sauce,

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:23.080
and it's gonna give it a
beautiful shine and glisten

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.864
as well as make it taste amazing.

00:08:24.864 --> 00:08:26.230
I'm gonna melt the butter in the pan.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.720
This may look like a lot of garlic,

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:28.780
but once you cook garlic,

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:31.640
it goes really sweet and
juicy and caramelized.

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:34.050
And that'll take out
some of that sharp bite.

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:35.760
That already smells so good.

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:38.780
The more garlic, the better.
You cannot have enough garlic.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:40.460
Now the garlic's nice and cooked out,

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:42.420
I'm gonna add a sprinkling of parsley.

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:44.100
We take up the heat, stir it in.

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:46.350
So now this is ready, I'm just
gonna pull this in the jug.

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:49.440
And this will be our fountain receptacle.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:51.350
Let me set this aside and build our tower.

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:52.320
So I have this cone,

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:54.360
which I think will provide
the structural integrity

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:57.370
that we need, as well as
giving it a harmonious look.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:58.710
So I'm gonna use these toothpicks

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:01.790
and then pressing the
dough ball on like so.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:02.980
Oh, yeah. That works.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:07.240
So my system is winging
it. I'm just winging it.

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:10.380
And I'm hoping that it's not gonna crumble

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:11.626
under the pressure.

00:09:11.626 --> 00:09:13.860
I'm hoping that I'm not gonna
crumble under the pressure.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:15.670
It's kind of like doing a puzzle,

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:17.800
an edible, delicious puzzle.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:19.880
Hey, and that's our first row done.

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:22.740
I feel like I should have
done some more calculations

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:24.500
before starting the build.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:26.800
Oh, no. We have our first casualty.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:28.900
The bottom row has collapsed.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:30.870
I think this is a toothpick issue.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.320
I think this is an easy solve.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:35.900
I'm just gonna put it back
and hope for the best.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:38.760
Okay, nothing that can't
be solved with a toothpick.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.810
So this isn't as easy as it looks.

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:43.290
I'm actually having to
think about the exact ball

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:44.650
to go in the exact right place.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.559
It's a bit of a game of Tetris.

00:09:46.559 --> 00:09:48.820
(game music)

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:53.570
It's looking so good. It's
exceeded my expectations so far.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:56.520
I feel like it can only
get better from here.

00:09:56.520 --> 00:10:00.630
So I started by using
these half toothpicks,

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:02.360
and then they just kept falling out.

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:07.220
So we've gone full whack with
the full length toothpick,

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:08.470
and that's working really well just

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:10.670
to keep them nice and stable.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:12.244
It seems to be going to plan.

00:10:12.244 --> 00:10:13.400
I feel like this is Everest

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:15.260
and we've nearly reached the summit.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:18.620
I just hope I don't get
altitude poisoning near the top.

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:20.200
So close!

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:22.840
It's really satisfying
that the taller you get,

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:24.960
the less dough balls you
need to complete a row.

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:29.960
I would show up to a party with
two of these under my arms.

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:31.890
Keep the party going all night.

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:33.900
Three or four more rows.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:36.210
This has been a real journey.

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:39.590
It's been an exploration of myself.

00:10:39.590 --> 00:10:41.610
I've gotten to know my levels of patience.

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:44.440
I feel like my energy
levels are waning now.

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:45.580
I'm gonna have to eat some dough balls

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.080
to have the stamina to finish.

00:10:48.536 --> 00:10:49.369
Mmm!

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:52.640
Okay, the final rose.

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:53.570
You think you're close

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:56.880
and then you realize no, you're
not actually not that close.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:58.620
This has like 200 balls on this thing,

00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:01.120
but this is great for
any celebrations of life.

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:04.470
Weddings, birthdays, anniversaries...

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:06.400
The final row.

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:08.713
The star on top of the Christmas tree.

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:13.490
So the assembly is done, but
we're not quite finished.

00:11:13.490 --> 00:11:15.540
We're gonna add the
delicious garlic butter

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:19.750
and turn this baby into a
flowing fountain of decadence.

00:11:19.750 --> 00:11:22.840
I'm gonna slowly pour
the butter over the top

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:25.510
and hope it gets a nice even covering

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:27.780
I'm nervous because
there's only one chance

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:28.810
to do this right.

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:30.180
Here it goes.

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:34.060
(suspenseful classical music)

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:36.740
Oh my God.

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:39.590
Wow! That does look really good.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:40.710
Think I'm gonna go in with a brush

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:43.130
and just make sure
everything is nicely coated.

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:46.410
I feel like this has gone a
lot better than I anticipated.

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:48.550
It looks really epic.

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:51.400
I feel like I'm in the
presence of a great beauty.

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:55.480
The Mona Lisa, the
leaning tower of cheese-a.

00:11:57.114 --> 00:12:00.513
And it's gonna look even better
when I add my cheese crisps.

00:12:00.513 --> 00:12:02.100
(mellow jazz music)

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:04.120
So now we have our parmesan crisps.

00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:06.150
They're gonna go into cute little flowers

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:07.970
and go in all these gaps.

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:10.420
Hey, just folding them up into flowers

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:13.780
and then finding a space on
the tower to pop them in.

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:15.570
Stay.

00:12:15.570 --> 00:12:17.410
I'm just gonna go all the way around,

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:19.680
decorating wherever there's a space.

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:21.010
This is really adding texture

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.400
which elevates the whole thing.

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:24.140
If you have a spare 24 hours,

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:26.770
I definitely think you
should try this at home.

00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:28.300
So it's really coming together.

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:30.500
It is so much better than I expected.

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:33.000
I did not know that I was capable

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:35.400
of making this cheesy croquembouche.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:37.000
This has been an adventure.

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:39.803
And now the final parm crisp.

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:46.290
Tada! What a beauty. I've
done it. I'm a genius.

00:12:47.110 --> 00:12:50.620
The first ever savory,
cheesy croquembouche.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:52.530
I'm so excited to give it a try.

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:55.023
So let's see if it tastes
as good as it looks.

00:12:56.610 --> 00:12:57.443
Mm!

00:12:58.821 --> 00:13:00.424
Mmmm!

00:13:00.424 --> 00:13:01.304
Mm!

00:13:01.304 --> 00:13:02.137
That's so good.

00:13:02.137 --> 00:13:04.320
It's like a pizza in a ball.

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:07.230
It's fluffy. It's fresh. It's garlicy.

00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:08.660
This dough is perfect.

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:11.620
It just pulls right apart,
and it's so soft inside

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:13.100
with the perfect crunch on the outside.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:16.150
And that garlic butter is just stunning.

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:17.520
I almost don't wanna eat this

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:20.680
because it just looks
so great, but I will.

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:22.520
I'm gonna bag this up and take it home

00:13:22.520 --> 00:13:24.210
with me all the way back to England

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:25.620
to share with my friends there.

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:28.280
Just kidding. I'm gonna share
it with all my friends here.

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:29.760
Thanks so much for watching, guys.

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:31.070
This was so much fun.

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:32.640
Check me out on Buzzfeed UK.

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:36.408
I've been AmyTasty. Until next time. Bye!

00:13:36.408 --> 00:13:38.991
(upbeat music)

